<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 29.1 percent of their 1996/97 wheat by December 6, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Maize sowing reached 80 percent of total intended area. Recent rains were very timely for the maize, especially in Cordoba, Santa Fe and Entre Rios where the crop was flowering. Soybean sowing reached 48.5 percent of intentions, aided by the rain. Soy area should be 5.4 percent higher than last season. Cotton sowing reached 71.2 percent of intentions. Sunflower sowing was 90.6 percent over and had finished everywhere but in Buenos Aires, La Pampa and Cordoba.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,873  100.0(100.0) 1,943.4   29.1  (27.5)   (18.9)</p>
<p> Maize     3,794   80.0 (84.2)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,313   48.5 (60.2)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,004   90.6 (92.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     770   62.5 (65.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	989   71.2  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
